{"id": "De1B23eRO3l", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Young Dasharatha killed a boy by mistake. Years later, it killed HIM 💔 The King's Curse | Ramayan Part 3 of 12\n\n🏹 Ram left for the forest with Sita and Lakshman. All Ayodhya wept, and the old king ran after the chariot. Days later, the charioteer came back. Alone. (Ayodhya Kanda 40, 57)\n🌧️ That night, Dasharatha told queen Kausalya a secret. As a prince, he had a rare skill: hitting a target by sound alone. One rainy night by the Sarayu, he heard a sound, like an elephant drinking. He shot. And a boy cried out.\n🏺 A young ascetic, filling a pot for his blind parents. \"Take them this water,\" he said, and died. (Ayodhya 63)\n🥀 His parents asked, \"Son, why so quiet?\" And the prince had to tell them the truth. The father cursed him: \"You too will die grieving for your son.\" (Ayodhya 64)\n🤯 And back then, Dasharatha had no son at all.\n🪔 Now, crying for Ram, the king died that very night.\n\n➡️ Part 4: in the forest, a crow attacks Sita, and Ram picks up a blade of grass. Follow @therishikatha so you don't miss it!\n\n📚 Rishi Katha picture books tell our gods' stories for kids, in simple words and bright pictures. Insta Family Sale on Books 1–3, till 25 Oct → rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\n💬 Comment JAI SHRI RAM if you're watching the whole series 🙏\n🔖 Save this, and share it with someone who loves the Ramayan\n\n#ramayan #ramayana #dasharatha #shravankumar #kausalya #valmikiramayana #jaishriram #shriram #sanatandharma #ramayanseries #kidsbooks #rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792740872, "like_count": 2435, "comment_count": 30, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1109346465408699a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 54.521, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-2.fna.f